age>187</fpage><lpage>199</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9526190</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Smith1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Boni</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Laxminarayan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><source>Disease Evolution: Models, Concepts, and Data Analyses</source><publisher-loc>Providence, Rhode Island</publisher-loc><publisher-name>American Mathematical Society</publisher-name><fpage>213</fpage><lpage>237</lpage><comment>volume 71, chapter Dynam-ics and control of antibiotic resistance in                        structured metapopulations</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Smith2"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Dushoff</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Perencevich</surname><given-names>EN</given-names></name><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Levin</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Persistent colonization and the spread of antibiotic resistance                        in nosocomial pathogens: resistance is a regional problem.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><volume>101</volume><fpage>3709</fpage><lpage>3714</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14985511</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Levins1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Levins</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>1969</year><article-title>Some demographic and genetic consequences of environmental                        heterogeneity for biological control.</article-title><source>Bull Entomol Soc Am</source><volume>71</volume><fpage>237</fpage><lpage>240</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Kaplan1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaplan</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Drug resistance in nematodes of veterinary importance: a status                        report.</article-title><source>Trends Parasitol</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>477</fpage><lpage>481</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15363441</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Brent1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brent</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hollomon</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Fungicide resistance in crop pathogens: how can it be managed?</article-title><comment>Technical report, Fungicide Resistance Action Committee</comment></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Tabashnik1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tabashnik</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name><name><surname>Carriere</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Dennehy</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Morin</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sisterson</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Insect resistance to transgenic bt crops: Lessons from the                        laboratory and field.</article-title><source>Journal Of Economic Entomology</source><volume>96</volume><fpage>1031</fpage><lpage>1038</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14503572</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Parnell1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parnell</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>van den Bosch</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilligan</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Large-scale fungicide spray heterogeneity and the regional spread                        of resistant pathogen strains.</article-title><source>Phytopathology</source><volume>96</volume><fpage>549</fpage><lpage>555</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18944316</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Parnell2"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parnell</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilligan</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>van den Bosch</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Small-scale fungicide spray heterogeneity and the coexistence of                        resistant and sensitive pathogen trains.</article-title><source>Phytopathology</source><volume>95</volume><fpage>632</fpage><lpage>639</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18943779</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Comins1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Comins</surname><given-names>HN</given-names></name></person-group><year>1977</year><article-title>The development of insecticide resistance in the presence of                        migration.</article-title><source>J Theor Biol</source><volume>64</volume><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>97</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">556789</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Mani1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mani</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>Evolution of resistance with sequential application of                        insecticides in time and space.</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B</source><volume>238</volume><fpage>245</fpage><lpage>276</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2575753</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Lenormand1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lenormand</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Raymond</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Resistance management: the stable zone strategy.</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B</source><volume>265</volume><fpage>1985</fpage><lpage>1990</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Vacher1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vacher</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Bourguet</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Rousset</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Chevillon</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Hochberg</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Modelling the spatial configuration of refuges for a sustainable                        control of pests: a case study of bt cotton.</article-title><source>J Evol Biol</source><volume>16</volume><fpage>378</fpage><lpage>387</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14635838</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Haldane1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haldane</surname><given-names>JBS</given-names></name></person-group><year>1948</year><article-title>The theory of a cline.</article-title><source>J Genet</source><volume>48</volume><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>284</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18905075</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-May1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>May</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Endler</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>McMurtrie</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name></person-group><year>1975</year><article-title>Gene frequency clines in the presence of selection opposed by                        gene ow.</article-title><source>Am Nat</source><volume>109</volume><fpage>659</fpage><lpage>676</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Nagylaki1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nagylaki</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>1975</year><article-title>Conditions for the existence of clines.</article-title><source>Genetics</source><volume>80</volume><fpage>595</fpage><lpage>615</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1232026</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Slatkin1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Slatkin</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>1973</year><article-title>Gene ow and selection in a cline.</article-title><source>Genetics</source><volume>75</volume><fpage>733</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4778791</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Nagylaki2"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nagylaki</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><year>1978</year><article-title>Clines with asymmetric migration.</article-title><source>Genetics</source><volume>88</volume><fpage>813</fpage><lpage>827</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17248820</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pcbi.1000337-Lenormand2"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lenormand</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-g